From 52503d9f82f70239ac312714803eb3d5e7290254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:45:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] x86: decide header ISA requirements where the body is
 inlined

A callee without target(...) is now judged by what its IR depends on,
recorded during lowering in IrFunction::x86_isa_needs:

* relied: features whose permission check passed. Such a body inlines only
  into callers holding them; ISA-neutral IR (e.g. _mm_popcnt_u32's
  __builtin_popcount) inlines anywhere and is lowered under the final
  function's features. This fixes the target("arch=x86-64") popcnt leak:
  the call stayed out of line and the -mpopcnt copy ran on a v1 path.
* FP/SIMD bodies never move into general-regs-only, no-sse2 or no-80387
  callers (isa::function_x87_denial, now shared with the final-text check).
* deferred: lcccsimd.h's 512-bit intrinsics are always_inline bodies without
  GCC's per-function target. A plain always_inline body records what its
  unit lacks; inlining settles what the caller grants (X86IsaNeeds::absorb)
  and any survivor is an error before code generation with GCC's verdict
  ("inlining failed in call to 'always_inline' ...: target specific option
  mismatch"), naming every missing extension. target("avx512bw") callers
  now get vpaddb %zmm at -O0 and -O2; plain -march=x86-64 callers are
  rejected as GCC rejects them (the old tree compiled them, fail-open).

Also moves find_inline_call_sites' doc comment back onto its function (it
had been attached to target_isa_allows_inline since upstream inserted that
function between them).

Tests: target_isa_tests (plain callee needs, deferred settlement, absorb
masking); check_intrinsic_feature_gate.sh plain/granting/nested 512-bit
cases at -O0 and -O2. The feature and target-attribute gates, which failed
on the previous commit, pass.
