From bdab682b554c46b3fcac6b56a794d716577e0e4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:46:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/17] cpu_supports: accept GCC 16.2's whole ISA_NAMES_TABLE

Measured: 16 names GCC 16.2 accepts were compile errors in lccc, among
them the x86-64-v2/v3/v4 level checks dispatchers use, avx512bmm, apxf and
the AMX-FP8/TF32/AVX512/MOVRS family. The census never caught them because
its candidate list was hand-picked (it also lacked bmi, bmi2, adx, lm, ...).

* New probe words: CPUID 0x19 EBX (aeskle, widekl), 0x1E.1 EAX (amx-fp8,
  amx-tf32, amx-avx512, amx-movrs), 0x80000021 EAX (avx512bmm), and the
  synthetic IsaLevels word computed after the xstate gates from ISA_LEVELS,
  libgcc's exact level conditions. cmpxchg8b, ibt, 3dnowp, fxsave (alias
  of fxsr) read existing words; apxf gets the APX xstate gate (XCR0 bit 19).
* kl/widekl now read as clear unless the OS enabled Key Locker (AESKLE), as
  libgcc decides; before, kl answered 1 from the leaf-7 bit alone.
* avx512bmm is gated on the AVX-512 xstate. libgcc omits the check for this
  one bit, which would report ZMM code usable on an OS that does not save
  ZMM state.
* The test-only FEATURE_TABLE (src/common/isa_features.rs) is replaced by
  the driver model's own enums (X86Feature::ALL, X86ExtraFeature::ALL); the
  hand list had already drifted (no avx512bmm).
* scripts/cpu_supports_name_census.py: the candidates cover GCC's
  ISA_NAMES_TABLE; --gcc-isas fails when a GCC header has a name the list
  lacks. Census regenerated (Godbolt gcc16.2/clang): GCC accepts 116 names,
  all accepted by lccc.

check_cpu_supports_runtime.sh: LCCC and GCC agree on all 116 names on the
executing host (AVX-512 Xeon) under the default target, -march=x86-64-v3
and -march=raptorlake; the i686 probe agrees too.
