From afa3f92863364d16336bd3388b9bb39841196e6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:22:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] i686 lccc-ld: local symbols have file scope; local
 IFUNCs

Since 5bef1ab6d the linker has entered every STB_LOCAL definition into the
global symbol table as a 'fallback for glibc static archives'. That
commit has no reproducer, archive extraction never consulted it
(locals_and_weak_undefs_never_drive_extraction), and ELF gives locals
file scope. Measured against GNU ld:
- extern helper() linked silently against another file's static
  helper; GNU ld reports an undefined reference;
- a static atoi() captured every object's calls to libc's atoi: the
  program printed '99 99' where GNU ld's prints '5 99';
- a local marked a same-named global for PLT/COPY and routed local
  calls through that global's PLT;
- GOT slots were keyed by name, so local@GOT failed whenever a global
  of that name existed;
- STB_LOCAL IFUNCs were never given IPLT stubs, and dynamic links
  collected no IFUNCs at all. Calls and pointers returned the
  resolver's address.

Now:
- locals resolve only within their object;
- R_386_GOT32/GOT32X against a local gets a slot keyed by (object,
  symbol), unless GOT32X relaxes it;
- each local IFUNC gets an IPLT stub, which every reference (calls,
  data pointers, GOT slots) resolves to;
- R_386_IRELATIVE goes in .rel.iplt for static links and at the end of
  .rel.dyn for dynamic ones, as in the x86-64 emitter.

Tests: linker case i386_local_symbols_have_file_scope (all five, static
and dynamic, against ld.bfd; it fails on the previous binary) and unit
test locals_never_satisfy_other_objects_references. Full linker suite
312/312 and corpus 1235/0.
