new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e2be54ca7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-10-27-s83-series.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# S83 series follow-up (rebased onto 9fcf641e8, #990)
+
+Base: `ms178/lccc` main `9fcf641e8`. Every entry was reproduced before
+the fix and re-measured after it. Unless stated otherwise, the reference
+oracles are GCC 16.2, Clang 23.1.4 and ld.bfd/GAS 2.47.
+
+## Changes in this series
+
+| Area | Defect (measured) | Fix and evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| `__builtin_cpu_is` | Only a subset of GCC 16.2's names was accepted | All 73 names from libgcc's `processor_types`/`processor_subtypes` tables, generated by `scripts/gen_x86_cpu_is_table.py` (`--check` in CI). Gate `check_cpu_is_runtime.sh` 17/17 |
+| `pow2_cmov` (#985) | Liveness was over-conservative: `-O2` corpus +108 instructions vs pre-#985 | `FileLiveness` query; corpus asm A/B back to identical |
+| DWARF | No CU when only line rows were synthesised; the #985 gate failed on `SHF_COMPRESSED` input | One DWARF 4 CU per line unit; in-tree `inflate`/`zstd` decoders (1386/1386 harness; Callgrind 4 MB: inflate 110 M Ir vs zlib 75 M, zstd 121.9 M vs libzstd 69 M) |
+| i686 executable | No section-header table or debug sections; REL addends of debug relocations dropped; `PROVIDE` symbols overrode input definitions; COPY slots aligned to 4 | Complete SHT, static debug relocation, `.symtab`; gdb resolves file:line on `-m32`. Linker cases `i386_section_headers_and_debug`, `i386_provided_symbols_yield_to_inputs`, `i386_copy_relocation_alignment` |
+| i686 linker: local symbols | An `STB_LOCAL` definition was entered into the global table as a "fallback" (`5bef1ab6d`, no reproducer). Another file's `static helper` silently satisfied `extern helper` (GNU: undefined reference). A `static atoi` captured libc's `atoi` (`99 99`, GNU `5 99`). `local@GOT` hit a hard error whenever a global shared the name. IFUNCs printed resolver addresses in dynamic links, and in static links when called through a pointer | Locals are file-scoped. GOT slots for locals are keyed by (object, symbol). Local IFUNCs get IPLT stubs, used by every reference; IRELATIVE lives in `.rel.iplt` (static) or at the end of `.rel.dyn` (dynamic), mirroring x86-64 `emit_exec.rs`. Case `i386_local_symbols_have_file_scope` FAILS on the previous binary and PASSES now; unit test `locals_never_satisfy_other_objects_references` |
+| Script mode (x86-64) | DWARF/`.comment` orphans dropped; duplicate orphans not merged; no `__start_`/`__stop_`; `-s` kept `.symtab` | bfd parity; `script_orphans_match_gnu` |
+| `-g` invariance | `-g` changed code (x86-64 36/29/19 files at -O1/-O2/-O3; i686 26/54/60) through `.loc` rows inside peephole windows | `.loc` hidden as a no-op and re-emitted; opening row post-peephole; `dead_stores` window fixed. Gate `check_debug_info_invariance.sh` (292 compilations) in fast local CI and the `backend` job |
+| `fp_const_hoist`, i686 `else_hoist_diamonds` | Slot reuse / `.loc`-blind matchers | Fixed; `-O2` asm byte-identical over 2093 files, `-O0` 4 files smaller |
+| CI: trapv matrix (#988) | Hosted runs took 1,999 s / 1,953 s for the two legs, ~1.4 s locally. 910 expected SIGABRTs per leg each went through the runner's `core_pattern` pipe handler. Reproduced with a 50 ms handler: 50.7 s = 910 × 55 ms | #990 landed the same root-cause fix independently (`PR_SET_DUMPABLE` in the parent, verified with `PR_GET_DUMPABLE`). It is better than this series' per-child call, which was dropped in the rebase. #990 left the lane plan at 535 s per leg, so the three frontend shards would have run ~90/~90/~620 s. The lane was re-split by `scripts/ci_lane_split.py` (join + 3-way split) with the trapv legs at 2.0 s: 269/269/269 s predicted, 0.1 % imbalance |
+| `ensure_binutils_247_binary.sh` (#988) | `--verify-only` accepted any banner containing `2.47`, including 2.47.50.* (a binutils master snapshot), 2.470 and 2.47.1 | Uses `oracle_require_version` (whole release token on the identity line) |
+
+## Red-team verdicts on upstream work
+
+**#985.** Agree with: `is_opaque_control_transfer`, `lea_add_fuse`, the C23
+defaults, `return_home`, and the `identical_blocks` logic. Disagree with:
+- the `pow2_cmov` liveness (over-conservative; fixed);
+- the `.loc` unit test, which encoded a `-g` artifact (rewritten);
+- the i686 `parse.rs` leniency, a misdiagnosis of compressed input (now
+  strict, with decompression).
+
+**#988.** Agree with:
+- the content-addressed agent cache and the offline freshness gate (its own
+  self-tests and `test_agent_toolchain_cache.py`/`test_toolchain_cache.py`
+  pass, 19/19);
+- verifying mold 3.0.0 by SHA-256 and a real link probe;
+- the `kver`+pins build stamp for kernel `relocs`;
+- splitting the trapv matrix into one script per ABI. The coverage is
+  unchanged: all 6,776 cases per ABI, and the 910-trap total still pinned.
+
+Disagree with the cost model behind the three-shard frontend split. The
+1,130 s was the core-dump handler, not the matrix, and the measured shards
+ran 2,177/2,137/619 s against the 623 s each that the commit message
+claimed. The 2.47.50 snapshot string in the restore self-test fixture is
+cosmetic. The real lock pins the 2.47 release tarball (`154ab23b…`, the
+same bytes as `ensure_gas_247.sh`).
+
+## Open items
+
+- `__builtin_cpu_is`: GCC folds to one `cmpl` on `__cpu_model`. lccc adds
+  an init guard (kept: libgcc's `constructor(101)` races user priority-101
+  constructors) but neither shrink-wraps the guard's cold call nor hoists
+  the `__cpu_model` load out of loops.
+- The AArch64 and RISC-V linkers do not carry debug sections into their
+  outputs.
