classified as a deleted line before the first pass and re-emitted before
the next kept line (peephole_common::{hide_debug_rows,
join_with_debug_rows}). Two AArch64 passes, fuse_and_cmp_zero and
fold_zext_move_chains, required strict physical adjacency. They now step
over deleted lines, which also lets them fire after earlier deletions
without -g (range_check_fold.c at -O2 kept `and; cmp #0`).

