From a332678bac404d4025ee32644e15cea9be5e4f46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:18:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] x86 peephole: drop the relays jump threading orphans

jump_thread retargets `jle .LBB3` past an empty `.LBB3: jmp .LBB2` relay
but kept the relay. After a `ret` nothing can reach it, leaving dead
bytes: 4 such blocks in 22 bench files at -O0 (0 at -O2, where the IR
CFG cleanup runs first).

The pass kept every label because of computed gotos and address
identity. Both concern only labels a program can name, so a relay is now
dropped only when all of these hold:
- no live line anywhere in the file mentions its label (jump tables and
  `&&label` live in the same text; comments count too);
- the label is defined once and is not pinned;
- the line before it is an unconditional transfer (jmp, ret, ud2), so no
  fallthrough enters it;
- it holds exactly one direct `jmp`, after optional unreferenced alias
  labels and inert comments.
Compiler `LCCC_` markers stop the match. CFI is derived after the
peephole from the edges that remain, so the next live label still gets
its restore.

-O0: 0 dead relays (was 4). -O2 assembly is byte-identical over the same
22 files. -g invariance gate: 333/333.
